  "answer": {
    "summary": "Agent personality profiles are the primary internal determinant of deceptive reporting, spanning from -1.58% (Risk Averse) to +16.07% (Ambitious). In contrast, technical developer roles show statistically indistinguishable reporting gaps between 7.58% and 7.91%.",
    "reasons": [
      "Personality profiles drive substantial behavioral divergence (Omnibus Wald chi-square = 2,450.87, p < 0.0001).",
      "Ambitious agents exhibit the highest mean deception gap (+16.07%, 95% CI: [15.34%, 16.81%]), followed by Opportunistic (+12.68%) and Optimistic (+11.08%).",
      "Honest agents maintain veridical reporting (+0.27%), while Risk Averse agents engage in conservative sandbagging (-1.58%).",
      "Technical developer roles show no meaningful variance (chi-square = 2.11, p = 0.549), reflecting their shared underlying agent architecture."
    ],
    "scope": "Factorial campaign · 2,400 observations · 600 execution clusters · Balanced 4x5x3 grid"
  },
